                        {
                          "String": "/HUMAN EXPOSURE STUDIES/ In a repeated insult patch test (RIPT), 200 human volunteers were tested for contact sensitization of a purple wax cosmetic formulation containing 5.0% oleic acid. Nine 24-hr closed induction patches containing 0.3 mL of the formulation were applied to sites on the volar forearm on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Fridays of 3 consecutive weeks during the induction phase of the study. Signs of irritation were scored 48 or 72 hr after the application. After a 10-14 day nontreatment period, a single 48-hr challenge patch was made to a separate site, and the site was scored 48-hr and 72-hr to 96-hr after application. Of the 200 subjects, 153 completed the study. Slight irritation was observed in 1 to 3 subjects during the induction phase, and 1 subject reacted slightly to the challenge patch after 48 hr. \"No contact sensitization\" was produced by the formulation under the conditions of this study.",
